Kind: `[[ component.kind ]]`[% if component.command %] — command: `[[ component.command | join(" ") ]]`[% endif %]

| Key | Default | Role |
|---|---|---|
| `[[ component.name ]].enabled` | `true` | Enables or disables the component entirely. |
| `[[ component.name ]].replicaCount` | `[[ component.replicas ]]` | Number of replicas, overridden per environment. |
| `[[ component.name ]].image.repository` | `[[ component.image_repository ]]` | Repository of the image, without the registry. |
| `[[ component.name ]].image.tag` | `[[ domain.image.tag or "\"\"" ]]` | Tag of the image; empty, it falls back on `appVersion`. |
| `[[ component.name ]].image.pullPolicy` | `[[ domain.image.pull_policy ]]` | Pull policy of the image. |
| `[[ component.name ]].containerPort` | `[[ component.container_port ]]` | Port listened to by the container. |
| `[[ component.name ]].portName` | `[[ component.port_name ]]` | Name of the port, taken up by the Service and the probes. |
[% if component.has.service %]
| `[[ component.name ]].service.enabled` | `true` | Creates the Service or not. |
| `[[ component.name ]].service.type` | `[[ component.service.type ]]` | `ClusterIP`, `NodePort` or `LoadBalancer`. |
| `[[ component.name ]].service.port` | `[[ component.service.port ]]` | Port exposed by the Service. |
[% endif %]
[% if component.has.ingress %]
| `[[ component.name ]].ingress.enabled` | `true` | Publishes the component outside the cluster or not. |
| `[[ component.name ]].ingress.className` | `[[ component.ingress.class_name ]]` | Targeted controller; never double it with the `kubernetes.io/ingress.class` annotation. |
| `[[ component.name ]].ingress.host` | `""` | Host served; set by each `values-<env>.yaml`, empty the Ingress is omitted. |
| `[[ component.name ]].ingress.path` | `[[ component.ingress.path ]]` | Path served by the rule. |
| `[[ component.name ]].ingress.pathType` | `[[ component.ingress.path_type ]]` | `Exact`, `Prefix` or `ImplementationSpecific`; mandatory field. |
| `[[ component.name ]].ingress.tls.enabled` | `[[ component.ingress.tls | to_yaml ]]` | Terminates TLS; at `false` the `tls` block disappears entirely. |
| `[[ component.name ]].ingress.tls.issuer` | `[[ component.ingress.issuer ]]` | cert-manager ClusterIssuer issuing the certificate. |
| `[[ component.name ]].ingress.tls.secretName` | `""` | Secret carrying the certificate; empty = `<resource>-tls`. |
| `[[ component.name ]].ingress.annotations` | `{}` | Annotations specific to the controller. |
[% endif %]
| `[[ component.name ]].probes.enabled` | `[[ component.probes.enabled | to_yaml ]]` | Enables the liveness and readiness probes. |
| `[[ component.name ]].probes.liveness.path` | `[[ component.probes.liveness_path ]]` | HTTP path of the liveness probe. |
| `[[ component.name ]].probes.readiness.path` | `[[ component.probes.readiness_path ]]` | HTTP path of the readiness probe. |
| `[[ component.name ]].probes.startup.enabled` | `[[ component.probes.startup_enabled | to_yaml ]]` | Startup probe, for a slow application. |
| `[[ component.name ]].resources.requests.cpu` | `[[ component.resources.cpu_request ]]` | CPU reserved by the scheduler. |
| `[[ component.name ]].resources.requests.memory` | `[[ component.resources.memory_request ]]` | Memory reserved by the scheduler. |
| `[[ component.name ]].resources.limits.cpu` | `[[ component.resources.cpu_limit ]]` | CPU ceiling, beyond which the container is slowed down. |
| `[[ component.name ]].resources.limits.memory` | `[[ component.resources.memory_limit ]]` | Memory ceiling, beyond which the container is killed. |
| `[[ component.name ]].podSecurityContext` | see `values.yaml` | Security context of the pod. |
| `[[ component.name ]].securityContext` | see `values.yaml` | Security context of the container. |
| `[[ component.name ]].nodeSelector` | `{}` | Placement constraint on the nodes. |
| `[[ component.name ]].tolerations` | `[]` | Tolerations to node taints. |
| `[[ component.name ]].affinity` | `{}` | Affinity and anti-affinity rules. |
| `[[ component.name ]].extraEnv` | `[]` | Additional environment variables. |
[% if component.has.configmap %]
| `[[ component.name ]].config.enabled` | `true` | Creates the ConfigMap and its injection into the container. |
| `[[ component.name ]].config.mountAs` | `[[ component.config["mount_as"] ]]` | `env` (via `envFrom`) or `file` (mounted under `mountPath`). |
